---
import FallCourseLayout from '../../layouts/FallCourseLayout.astro';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const fullHtml = readFileSync('public/pixel-pilot/starter/index.html','utf8');
const css = readFileSync('public/pixel-pilot/starter/style.css','utf8');
const html = fullHtml.match(/<body>([\s\S]*)<\/body>/)?.[1].trim() ?? '';
const pen = JSON.stringify({title:'Peel Up the Pixels — one deliberate change',description:'DESN 368. Inspect, predict, change, explain. Student AI-free opening exercise.',html,css,js:'',editors:'110',layout:'left'});
---
<FallCourseLayout title="Peel Up the Pixels — opening studio" wide>
  <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/1/">Course</a> / <a href="/1/weeks/week-0/">Opening studio</a></p>
  <section class="pilot-intro"><div><p class="course-course-title">45–60 minutes · Work with a partner · No AI</p><h1>There’s more<br/>under the surface.</h1><p class="page-intro">This invitation is made from a few elements and a handful of rules. Peel it back. Find what changes the thing you see.</p></div><p class="pilot-goal"><strong>Your goal</strong><br/>Point to one part of a page, find its source, change it on purpose, and explain the result.</p></section>
  <section class="pixel-lab" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
    <div class="lab-heading"><h2 id="lab-title">An invitation, taken apart.</h2><span>Look before you edit.</span></div>
    <div class="lab-tools" hidden><button type="button" id="structure-toggle" aria-pressed="false">Reveal HTML structure</button><button type="button" id="boxes-toggle" aria-pressed="false">Reveal CSS boxes</button><button type="button" id="size-toggle" aria-pressed="false">Compare a smaller heading</button><button type="button" id="reset-demo">Reset the example</button></div>
    <div class="lab-panels">
      <div class="preview-area"><article class="notice demo-notice" data-tag="article.notice"><p class="location demo-location" data-tag="p.location">Spokane, Washington</p><h1 class="demo-title" data-tag="h1">Meet me at the river.</h1><p data-tag="p">A small invitation to spend an afternoon outside. Bring a sketchbook. Notice one thing you usually walk past.</p><a href="#plan" data-tag="a">Make a plan</a><p id="plan" class="demo-plan" data-tag="p#plan">Choose a place, a time, and someone to invite.</p></article></div>
      <div class="source-area"><h3>The source beneath it</h3><p>HTML identifies the parts. CSS describes how those parts look.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="HTML for the invitation"><code>&lt;article class="notice"&gt;
  &lt;p class="location"&gt;Spokane, Washington&lt;/p&gt;
  <span class="html-line">&lt;h1&gt;Meet me at the river.&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
  &lt;p&gt;A small invitation…&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;a href="#plan"&gt;Make a plan&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;p id="plan"&gt;Choose a place…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;</code></pre><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="CSS for the article and heading"><code>.notice &#123;
  <span class="box-line">padding: 32px;
  border: 4px solid #172128;</span>
&#125;
.notice h1 &#123;
  <span class="size-line">font-size: <span id="code-size">48px</span>;</span>
&#125;</code></pre><p class="live-explanation" id="lab-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">The heading begins at 48px. Before using the controls, predict what a smaller value will change.</p></div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p class="callout">The interactive overlays need JavaScript. The source above, starter below, and full exercise still work. Compare the rendered invitation with its HTML, then change the starter manually.</p></noscript>
  </section>
  <section class="pilot-steps" id="your-turn">
    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">1</span><div><h2>Inspect and predict</h2><p><strong>10 minutes.</strong> With a partner, name the title, location, invitation text, and link. Find each in the HTML. Explain what the heading tag contributes.</p><p>Before comparing the smaller heading, finish this sentence aloud: “If <code>font-size</code> changes from <code>48px</code> to <code>32px</code>, I expect…” Then use the control and check your prediction.</p><p>Reveal the CSS boxes. Find the space between the article’s border and its content. That is padding. It belongs inside the box.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">2</span><div><h2>Make one deliberate change</h2><p><strong>20 minutes.</strong> Open the starter. CodePen’s HTML panel contains what belongs inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>; the downloaded file includes the full document. Put CSS in its own panel or keep the downloaded <code>style.css</code> beside <code>index.html</code>.</p><form action="https://codepen.io/pen/define/" method="post" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><input type="hidden" name="data" value={pen}/><button class="button" type="submit">Open the starter in CodePen</button></form><p class="muted">Opens a new tab with the supplied example. Sign in to your own CodePen account if you want to save a Pen. Nothing from your coursework is sent until you choose to open it.</p><ol><li>Run the unchanged starter and locate its heading.</li><li>Replace the invitation with a place or activity that matters to you. Keep one <code>h1</code>.</li><li>Find <code>.notice h1</code> in the CSS. Write a prediction, then change only <code>font-size</code> from <code>48px</code> to <code>32px</code>.</li><li>Compare the result. Undo the change, then redo it. Explain which result better suits your invitation.</li><li>Change the article’s <code>padding</code> from <code>32px</code> to <code>16px</code>. Identify what moved and what did not.</li></ol><p><strong>Stop here:</strong> your invitation contains your content, and you can explain both edits. More effects are optional, not required.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">3</span><div><h2>Explain it without help</h2><p><strong>10 minutes.</strong> Swap roles. One person points to an element; the other finds the HTML and the CSS rule that affects it. Explain a new prediction before touching the code.</p><ul><li>Which tag makes the title a heading?</li><li>Which selector changes that heading’s size?</li><li>What is the difference between changing text and changing padding?</li><li>Can you restore the original appearance without using AI?</li></ul><p>If a step is unclear, return to the original starter, change only one value, and ask your partner to describe the result. Ask the instructor about the first result you cannot explain.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">4</span><div><h2>Keep a small piece of evidence</h2><p><strong>5 minutes.</strong> Save one screenshot or working Pen link, the specific source line you changed, and two sentences: what you predicted and what happened. Add one question or next step.</p><p>Use the <a href="/1/weeks/week-0/">opening studio instructions</a> for submission. This is practice evidence, not an extra project.</p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="fallback"><h2>CodePen unavailable?</h2><p>Download both files into one folder, keeping their names. Open <code>index.html</code> in a browser and edit either file in a plain-text code editor. Save and refresh to see the result. You can also copy the source below into CodePen’s HTML and CSS panels.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button secondary" href="/pixel-pilot/starter/index.html" download="index.html">Download index.html</a><a class="button secondary" href="/pixel-pilot/starter/style.css" download="style.css">Download style.css</a></div><details><summary>Full HTML for CodePen</summary><pre tabindex="0"><code>{html}</code></pre></details><details><summary>Full CSS</summary><pre tabindex="0"><code>{css}</code></pre></details><p><strong>Delivery check:</strong> the page opens, the stylesheet loads, your heading is present, the link goes to the plan, and you can locate both edits in the source.</p></section>
  <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/1/weeks/week-0/">Return to the opening studio</a></div>
</FallCourseLayout>
<script>
  const lab = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.pixel-lab');
  const structure = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#structure-toggle');
  const boxes = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#boxes-toggle');
  const size = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#size-toggle');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#lab-status');
  const codeSize = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#code-size');
  const tools = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.lab-tools');
  if (lab && structure && boxes && size && status && codeSize && tools) {
    tools.hidden = false;
    function update() {
      const showingStructure = structure!.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true';
      const showingBoxes = boxes!.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true';
      const smaller = size!.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true';
      lab!.classList.toggle('show-structure', showingStructure);
      lab!.classList.toggle('show-boxes', showingBoxes);
      lab!.classList.toggle('smaller', smaller);
      codeSize!.textContent = smaller ? '32px' : '48px';
      status!.textContent = [showingStructure ? 'Labels identify the HTML elements.' : '',showingBoxes ? 'The blue area shows padding inside the article border. Dashed outlines show the content boxes.' : '', smaller ? 'The heading is now 32px. Its words and HTML tag have not changed.' : 'The heading is 48px.'].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
    }
    for (const button of [structure, boxes, size]) button.addEventListener('click', () => {button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', button.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true' ? 'false' : 'true'); update();});
    document.querySelector('#reset-demo')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{for(const button of [structure,boxes,size])button.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false');update();});
  }
</script>
<style>
  .pilot-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;align-items:end;gap:64px;margin-bottom:48px}.pilot-goal{border-top:4px solid #b8392d;padding-top:18px}.pixel-lab{border:2px solid #172128;background:#fff;box-shadow:10px 10px 0 #d0dadf;margin-bottom:60px}.lab-heading{padding:22px 28px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid #c9d1d5}.lab-heading h2{margin:0;font-size:27px}.lab-heading span{font-size:14px}.lab-tools:not([hidden]){display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;padding:18px 28px;border-bottom:1px solid #c9d1d5}.lab-tools button{cursor:pointer;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #172128;background:#fff;color:#172128;border-radius:3px;font-size:14px}.lab-tools button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#172128;color:#fff}.lab-tools #reset-demo{margin-left:auto;text-decoration:underline;border-color:transparent}.lab-panels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.preview-area{padding:40px;background:#e3e9ec;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.demo-notice{position:relative;max-width:520px;width:100%;padding:32px;background:#efc55b;border:4px solid #172128;color:#172128;font:18px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}.demo-notice p{margin:18px 0}.demo-notice .demo-location{font-size:14px}.demo-notice .demo-title{font:700 48px/1.05 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:32px 0}.demo-notice a{color:#172128;font-weight:700}.demo-plan{font-size:16px}.source-area{min-width:0;background:#172128;color:#e4eef0;padding:28px}.source-area h3{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:22px;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#fff}.source-area p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55}.source-area pre{overflow:auto;white-space:pre;font:12px/1.8 'DM Mono',monospace;border-top:1px solid #51616a;padding:18px 0;margin:15px 0}.source-area code{font:inherit}.source-area .live-explanation{border-left:3px solid #efc55b;padding-left:15px;margin-bottom:0}.show-structure [data-tag]{position:relative;outline:2px solid #09627b;outline-offset:6px}.show-structure [data-tag]::before{content:attr(data-tag);position:absolute;left:0;top:-18px;padding:1px 4px;background:#09627b;color:#fff;font:11px/1.3 'DM Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:0;white-space:nowrap;z-index:1}.show-structure .html-line{background:#075c75;color:#fff}.show-boxes .demo-notice{background:#b7dfe8}.show-boxes .demo-notice>*{background:#efc55b;outline:2px dashed #09627b}.show-boxes .box-line{background:#075c75;color:#fff}.smaller .demo-notice .demo-title{font-size:32px}.smaller .size-line{background:#075c75;color:#fff}.pilot-steps{max-width:850px}.step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:50px 1fr;gap:24px;padding:30px 0;border-top:1px solid #c9d1d5}.step-number{font:24px/1.2 'DM Mono',monospace;color:#b8392d;padding-top:4px}.step h2{margin:0 0 20px}.step code,.fallback code{font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.85em;background:#e2e9ec;padding:2px 4px}.step li{margin:12px 0}.fallback{background:#fff;border-top:4px solid #09627b;padding:24px 32px;max-width:850px;margin-top:30px}.fallback h2{margin-top:0}.fallback details{padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid #c9d1d5}.fallback summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}.fallback pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#e2e9ec;padding:20px;font-size:13px}.fallback pre code{padding:0}.fallback p{font-size:16px}
  @media(max-width:1000px){.lab-panels{grid-template-columns:1fr}.source-area pre{font-size:14px}.demo-notice{max-width:520px}.pilot-intro{gap:24px;grid-template-columns:1fr 220px}.lab-heading{align-items:start;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.pilot-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}.preview-area{padding:26px 16px}.pixel-lab{margin-right:8px}.lab-tools:not([hidden]),.lab-heading,.source-area{padding:18px}.source-area pre{font-size:11px}.step{grid-template-columns:30px 1fr;gap:12px}.fallback{padding:22px}.lab-tools #reset-demo{margin-left:0}}
  @media print{@page{margin:15mm}.pilot-intro{margin-bottom:18px}.pilot-intro h1{font-size:28pt}.pilot-intro .page-intro{font-size:12pt}.pilot-goal{font-size:10pt}.lab-heading{padding:12px}.lab-heading h2{font-size:15pt}.lab-tools{display:none!important}.lab-panels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.preview-area{background:#fff;padding:12px}.source-area{background:#eee;color:#000;padding:12px}.source-area pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:8pt}.source-area p{font-size:9pt}.source-area h3{color:#000}.pixel-lab{box-shadow:none;break-inside:avoid}.pilot-intro{display:block}.step{break-inside:avoid}.fallback details{display:block}.fallback details::details-content{content-visibility:visible;display:block}}
</style>
